@flexiarg buffer-cleaner/classify-staleness
@title Classify Staleness
@keywords classify, prior, needed-later, uncertainty, age
@audience adapter, G computation
@tone normative
@style pattern
@grade technique
@provenance v3 diagram chip 2; the genuinely-uncertain channel. Prior-over-needed-later as a function of age is the codex-26 finding made data: a stale-age threshold ENCODES a prior; we declare it instead of hiding it in a threshold.
@class process
@domain process
@status adapter node; params in nodes/classify-staleness.params.edn

! conclusion:
  Each candidate is classified {decisiveness, prior-needed-later,
  revisit-cost} from the category parameter table and, for the
  uncertain channel, from the age->prior map. Values carry :source.

  + HOWEVER: all current values are :constructed — the real cleaner
    cannot measure revisit rates (no identity/reopen history); the
    label travels with every number into G.

  + BECAUSE: the score is only as honest as its inputs are labeled.
